daharness (0.2.0) kali; urgency=medium

  [ 0.2.0 — the release of record ]

  * Executor dispatch hotfix (tagged into 0.2.0, 2026-10-30): the
    bare-instance builders of the standalone lane
    (daharness.executor._new_registry, replkit.core._make_executor)
    never gained the Phase-0 brain-session state, so every REPL
    dispatch — which announces the 'repl' identity — died with
    "AttributeError: 'ToolRegistry' object has no attribute
    '_brain_session_lock'" before the Brain socket was even consulted.
    The init is centralized in daharness.executor
    ._init_brain_session_state and every construction path (full
    __init__ + both bare builders) rides it; regression tests in
    tests/test_executor_standalone.py pin the lane.

  * Version 0.2.0: the +pkgNN build counter retires. The submission of
    record remains v0.1.0-submitted (0.1.0, 2026-10-22); every delta from
    there is the pkg1..pkg18 diary below, plus the two arcs that postdate
    pkg18 — the Rust ports and this packaging alignment — itemized here:

  * Rust lanes (rust/: three crates shipped as sources, not built at
    package time — no cargo Build-Depends, the build lane stays python+C):
    - rust/pcap: nano-pcap — standalone pcap codec/dissection/projection
      core (libpcap capture behind an optional feature). Fixed the
      dissector panics and header offsets, nano-pcap magic, >=1e9 ns
      carry into seconds, empty-load, sniff deadline, load limit,
      path-trust, and lock/fsync handling.
    - rust/scratch: complete port of utils/scratch_store.py (SQLite
      metadata + gzip payload files, agent-scoped opaque refs). Root-guard
      chown walk made symlink-proof; ScratchStore::open never chmods
      through a symlink. The python store mirrors the same hardening
      (sidecars 0600, symlinked files skipped) and gained
      tests/test_scratch_store_perms.py.
    - rust/brain: the in-progress Rust sidecar — transport/framing/typed
      dispatch (milestone 1), the Python tool-worker IPC seam (M2), the
      real registry + shared execution core in the worker (M3, riding the
      root module tool_exec.py), and the OS singleton dance (M4: flock,
      stale-socket unlink, per-lane umask). Tool execution, the registry,
      scope gate and tracker stay in Python by design; the python Brain
      (listeners/thebrain.py) is still the canonical sidecar — the rust
      lane is a documented alternative, not yet the service default.
    - CI: cargo fmt --check, clippy -D warnings and the crate test suites.

  * Packaging alignment (this release):
    - debian/rules ships rust/ crate sources under
      /usr/share/daharness/rust/ (target/ + crate-internal run/ excluded).
    - daharness-rust(1): the python/c -> python/rust upgrade lane —
      status probes offline, toolchain/build/smoke are explicit network
      steps (crate sources + Cargo.locks ship; builds land in the state
      root, never the package tree), brain runs the rust sidecar + its
      python tool-worker. Install stays isolated; nothing replaces the
      shipped python lanes.
    - daharness-index(1): the removed --chat/secretary lane (removed
      2026-10-20) is retired from the docs — python -m daharness.core
      accepts --clear only; the driving LLM is external.
    - daharness-tools(7): same correction, plus the engagement cobweb
      (journal/evidence/unknown ledger), job-log collection, and the
      fleet-scheduler/worker-queue courtesy layers.
    - daharness.service: Description and comments no longer reference the
      removed Chroma backend (SQLite + numpy vector store since 2026-10-20).
    - .env.example inventories the scale-lane knobs (FLEET_*,
      WORKER_QUEUE_*, BG_LOG_GC_*, BURP_FLEET_*, SNAPSHOT_*).
    - man pages re-synced to their markdown sources (daharness-pg(1) had
      drifted: HARNESS_DB_HOST bind-mirror, status lane).

  * Headline recap since v0.1.0-submitted (full detail in the entries
    below): ChromaDB replaced by the local SQLite + numpy vector store
    (no vendored wheels, network-isolated build); the pydantic-ai
    secretary chat lane removed (headless build, external driving LLM);
    the scale-doctrine Phases 0-3 substrate (agent identity, durable job
    store + log GC + launch roll-down, brain session ints, fleet
    scheduler, sqlmap/jadx/burp fleet adapters, worker queue with the RSS
    ledger); the engagement cobweb (journal + typed evidence store +
    unknown ledger, SQLite with the daharness-pg Postgres lane); the
    capability doctor; the execution-envelope contract; large-file
    module carves; per-thread vector-store connections; MSF RPC password
    rotation + orphan recovery; init.d hardening (root-only start/stop,
    crash logs, WSL mirrored-network guard); the swallowed-exception
    traceability pass.

 -- daharness packaging <vgreenwald@student.cnm.edu>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:37:00 -0600

daharness (0.1.0+pkg18) kali; urgency=medium

  * Traceability pass: silent except-pass logging + jadx_fleet tag fix
    (2026-10-30):
    - 99 broad `except Exception: pass` sites across 34 files now log
      `logging.getLogger(__name__).debug("swallowed exception in <fn>",
      exc_info=True)` instead of passing silently — invisible at default
      levels, traceable with a full traceback the moment the level is
      raised. `import logging` inserted where absent (after __future__
      imports). Narrow documented typed swallows (OSError/ImportError/
      NXDOMAIN close-and-cleanup races, control flow rather than error
      concealment) deliberately stay silent.
    - Stale "TODO: log instead of passing" comments retired
      (burp_mcp x3, listening, thebrain, responder_analog — all now log);
      intent comments ("bookkeeping must never break the poller" etc.)
      preserved alongside the new debug record. One author-declined site
      (collaborator _handle_http peer-socket wait_closed teardown,
      --- IGNORE ---) stays a bare pass.
    - AGENTS.md gains a "Swallowed exceptions" convention under
      Development Guidelines so new code doesn't regress to bare pass.
    - payloads/jadx_fleet.py: jadx_fleet / jadx_fleet_status /
      jadx_fleet_stop drop the non-canonical `recon.binary` tag
      (not in the frozen 13-bucket CANONICAL_TAGS vocabulary) and carry
      `["infra"]`, same as auxiliaries.jadx.* and the operator's
      judgment-call note in tool_tags.py. Embeddings refresh on the next
      `python -m daharness.core` re-index.


  * init.d crash-log fix + WSL mirrored-networking guard hint (2026-10-25):
    - start-stop-daemon --background hardcodes the detached child's stdio
      to /dev/null; the shell-level >>"$_CRASHLOG" only captured s-s-d's
      OWN output, so a python crash as daharness surfaced as a silent
      "failed" with an empty /var/log/daharness-start.log (observed on
      Parrot-WSL). Both init.d scripts now pass -O/--output (s-s-d
      >= 1.20.6): s-s-d opens the file itself as root pre-chuid (dpkg
      1.22.22 do_start(): open() before setgid/setuid, then dup2), so the
      log works with the privilege drop and a root-owned /var/log file.
    - daharness-kernel gains the same crash log
      (/var/log/daharness-kernel-start.log) + a log_failure_msg pointer.
    - _prelaunch_guard's no-unit refusal gains a WSL hint: mirrored
      networking shares loopback TCP across distros, so a sibling distro
      running the same stack reads as "foreign leftovers" (brain down,
      TCP members up) with no owning process in this PID namespace.
      Detected via /proc/sys/fs/binfmt_misc/WSLInterop.
    - init.d start gains --chdir /var/lib/daharness (both scripts), parity
      with the systemd units' WorkingDirectory=. Without it s-s-d chdirs
      to / and msfrpcd's Rails boot resolves its app root to "/"
      (find_root_with_flag("config.ru", ..., Dir.pwd) fallback), unshifting
      /lib into $LOAD_PATH — bootsnap's load-path scan then walks all of
      /usr/lib and dies EACCES on the first unreadable dir (WSL kernel
      modules' root-only lost+found). Reproduced: `cd / && ruby msfrpcd
      --help` crashes, `cd /var/lib/daharness && ruby msfrpcd --help`
      boots clean. Lane-shaped bug, not WSL-shaped — any systemd-less
      host with an unreadable dir under /usr/lib hits it.
    - init.d start/stop refuse non-root callers with one honest line
      (LSB exit 4) instead of a raw shell "Permission denied" on the
      root-owned crash log — the >>"$_CRASHLOG" redirect runs with the
      CALLER's privileges, so a non-root `service daharness restart`
      died on the redirect before s-s-d even ran (observed 2026-10-25;
      the sudo path was already clean). status stays non-root callable.

