  * selftest macro: redirect, don't disable, pytest's cache on unwritable
    trees (deb defect, VM round trip 2026-10-21). The root-owned branch
    passed -p no:cacheprovider while pyproject ships cache_dir = "run/
    pytest-cache" and addopts carries --strict-config: with the plugin
    disabled the ini key becomes unknown, pytest 9 escalates exactly that
    to a usage error at run's end — exit 4, zero tests collected, the
    operator sees "1 warning in 0.91s" + "ERROR: Unknown config option:
    cache_dir" and can read the deb selftest as green when the suite
    never ran (every -q selftest on the guinea pig collected nothing).
    The macro now passes -o cache_dir=<per-euid tmpdir> instead: plugin
    stays loaded (cache_dir stays a known option, strict-config satisfied),
    the install tree is still never written, --lf works across runs, and
    the suite actually executes on the deb lane.
  * OLLAMA_BASE_URL import-time alert removed; unset note moved to the
    knob's only live consumer. daharness.registry minted a normalized
    OLLAMA_BASE_URL constant + logged "unset" INFO on EVERY registry
    import (REPL, selftest, gateway, Brain boot — first line of the
    guinea pig selftest transcript), though nothing imported the constant:
    auxiliaries/framework_status.py:framework_health, the harness's only
    OLLAMA_BASE_URL consumer, already resolved the env itself at call
    time. The dead constant + both import-time logger.info calls are gone;
    framework_health's ollama subsystem detail now appends the
    unset→default pointer (EMBED_URL independence included) so the note
    surfaces exactly when the LLM lane is being looked at, not on every
