  * ghost-uid reinstall (deb defect, 2026-10-21 VM round trip): purge keeps
    /var/lib/daharness (operator state — correct) AND deletes the system
    user (correct), so a reinstall re-mints daharness under a NEW uid while
    the kept tree's deep dirs still carry the old one. systemd's
    StateDirectory= re-asserts only the TOP dir on every start, so the
    wrong-owner subtree survived postinst's top-level-only reconcile —
    observed: chroma's persisted sqlite under ghost-uid ownership opened
    read-only, the rust frontend panicked 31s after every spawn
    (pyo3 PanicException: "attempt to write a readonly database"),
    wait_for_chroma burned its full 30s budget polling a corpse, then
    api_gateway.run() died constructing ToolRegistry (chromadb's HttpClient
    handshakes IN ITS CONSTRUCTOR) and the WHOLE unit went failed — one
    stale subdirectory = no harness. Repairs, four lanes: postinst
    reconciles the ENTIRE state tree (find|chown ghost files to the
    re-minted identity — the healing the keep-state doctrine requires);
    wait_for_chroma short-circuits when the spawned sidecar process has
    already exited (dead processes cannot self-heal; cites the persist dir
    + the ACTUAL uid-scoped log path — the hard-coded /tmp/chroma.log
    pointer lied on every non-root lane) and stops blaming the wrong
    artifact; api_gateway.run() degrades instead of dying — registry=None
    boots the gateway so /health (now grading "degraded" vs "ok" with the
    remediation inline), scratch, memory, and the budget lane stay up while
    every registry consumer (REST + MCP search/execute) returns 503 with
    the same remediation daharness doctor chroma emits, self-healing when
    the backend returns; postrm's purge ledger now prints the ghost-uid
    note so the kept-state/deleted-uid trade-off is visible at purge time.
    Regression tests: dead-spawn short-circuit + timeout path under the new
    shim attrs.

