daharness (0.1.0+pkg6) kali; urgency=high

  * kernel lane (deb defect): the kernelspec was a silent NO-OP on every
    freshly installed deb — Jupyter frontends launch kernel.json argv
    (`python3 /usr/share/daharness/tool_repl.py --kernel ...`) BARE: no
    wrapper to export PYTHONPATH, and script-dir sitecustomize.py does not
    auto-import on py3.13/3.14 for absolute-script invocations (verified
    empirically) — so the vendored chromadb closure never armed and the
    kernel died at daharness/__init__ -> registry.py:22 `import chromadb`
    before any tool or cell ran. `python tool_repl.py --install-kernelspec`
    and the packaged wrappers worked (PYTHONPATH armed), which is why the
    deb selftest lane stayed green while every frontend launch
    (jupyter console --kernel daharness, nbconvert --execute,
    KernelManager) died. tool_repl.py now arms <tree>/vendor itself —
    same prepend-before-heavy-imports semantics as sitecustomize (vendored
    closure wins overlaps; inert when vendor/ is absent, so dev-tree lanes
    keep pristine behavior; idempotent, so wrapper-armed lanes insert
    nothing) — one mechanism, two carriers, and a comment cross-reference
    in sitecustomize.py to keep them in sync. Bonus repair semantics:
    since kernelspecs re-execute the shim file (python), STALE kernelspecs
    heal on the next apt upgrade without re-running --install-kernelspec.
    Regression tests (tests/test_vendor_arming.py): tree arming +
    idempotency, shim inert-without-vendor dev-tree behavior, subprocess
    probe of the exact kernelspec launch shape (skips when no vendor/ —
    dev lane; exercises the real arm on the deb selftest lane).
    (VM-lane lesson, observed on deb boots 2026-10-20)
  * config lane (deb defect): /etc/daharness/daharness.env advertised the
    engagement-Postgres knobs as a COMMENTED var block — a commented set
    reads exactly like the live credential set, and on a pkg6 deb an
    operator copied it for an extension connect and authenticated against
    passwords that exist nowhere (the real ones are random-generated by
    daharness-pg init into /etc/daharness/pg.env; endpoint host 127.0.0.1,
    port 5433, db harness, roles harness_operator/brain/gateway/repl_lane —
    the 001_roles.sh *_change_me strings are container-lane fallbacks only,
    never deb creds). The template now carries no Postgres knobs at all
    (prose pointer to pg.env only), daharness.env(5) states the same, and
    the stale .dpkg-old conffile carrying the old hint was cleared on the
    affected box. (observed 2026-10-20)
