daharness (0.1.0+pkg5) kali; urgency=high

  * index wrapper: `daharness-index --stubs` now exists — the IDE lane is a
    front-facing command instead of a provisioned scripts path. The stub
    generator (pyright .pyi + PEP 562 shim + builtins.pyi fork + ruff
    builtins, minted from the same discovery/alias pipeline for zero drift)
    ships at /usr/share/daharness/scripts/gen_repl_stubs.py and the wrapper
    ROUTES --stubs BEFORE the chroma/Ollama probes: stub generation is
    offline compute (static AST + dynamic import, no embedding backend), so
    a down registry or embed host never blocks it. A clean deb operator
    (no ~/.vscode-server, no wheel pyright) can still generate: the deb
    bundles a typeshed builtins.pyi fork source
    (scripts/pyright_typeshed_builtins.pyi, Pylance 2026.4.1 copy), the
    wheel candidate is is_file-guarded (a deb dist-packages layout crashed
    the source scan with FileNotFoundError), and generation still refuses
    loudly when genuinely nothing can produce a COMPLETE fork. --check
    compares content with the humans-only "Generated:" wall-clock stamp
    masked (minute-granularity stamps made every check STALE on rollover),
    and on a package install reports SKIP for the checkout-only
    dabooks/ruff.toml block instead of a lying STALE. Man page (THE STUB
    VIEW) + README document the stubPath wiring. (VM 2026-10-20)
  * kernel lane: `daharness-kernel --install-kernelspec` fed the
    '--install-kernelspec' flag into IPKernelApp (the wrapper hard-prepends
    --kernel, so the dispatch never saw the flag) and
    `daharness --install-kernelspec` died on argparse's invalid choice —
    the operator had no working kernelspec command outside
    `daharness-repl --install-kernelspec`, which nothing advertised.
    The wrapper shape (--kernel --install-kernelspec) is unambiguous —
    kernelspec frontends only append -f <connection_file> — and now routes
    to the spec installer; the services wrapper prints the kernel-lane
    redirect (rc 2) instead of the dead end; man pages (daharness-kernel
    INSTALLING THE KERNELSPEC, daharness OPTIONS), README and the
    tool_repl usage text document the deb command. (VM 2026-10-20)
  * doctor: the masscan probe graded the doctor lane's own SOCK_RAW
    attempt and could lie both ways — a setcap'd binary (cap_net_raw+ep)
    got "may fail at launch, not at probe" while the setcap'd launch runs
    fine from an unprivileged lane, and a privileged probe could
    green-light a scan lane it can't see. It now grades the way
    run_masscan actually launches (root euid, lane SOCK_RAW creatable, or
    an exec-effective cap_net_raw file capability decoded from the
    binary's security.capability xattr), names the deciding source in the
    reason, carries the per-source evidence in extra, and scopes the
    unavailable verdict to the doctor lane instead of overclaiming.
    (VM 2026-10-20)
  * doctor hard gate: `daharness doctor` (and the framework_doctor tool)
    now REFUSES lanes that do not share the framework state root — root,
    the root's owner, or a member of its group only (rc 77, message names
    the group and the fix). Same operator-lane command reported false
    downs across shared state (snapshot_cache etc.) while
    `sudo daharness doctor` was all green — a non-privileged lane probes
    blind, so it now gets the refusal instead of a lying report.
    (VM 2026-10-20)
  * doctor: the jadx apk drop-dir probe demanded the READ-ONLY package
    tree (/usr/share/daharness/apk via __file__ math) while postinst
    creates the state-root lane — on the deb this read jadx down no matter
    what the operator did. It now imports APK_TARGETS_ROOT from
    auxiliaries.jadx (the same WORKSPACE_ROOT-resolved lane the tool
    itself uses), mirroring _check_r2's BINARY_TARGETS_ROOT treatment;
    the remediation names JADX_APK_TARGETS_ROOT. (VM 2026-10-20)
  * -h: dropped the stale daharness-chroma epilog line ("manual/dev lane")
    — chroma is the daemon's first-class supervised sidecar now; the
    wrapper still ships as the unadvertised dev escape hatch.

