daharness (0.1.0+pkg3) kali; urgency=high

  * Shared-state permissions actually REACH the running units now: the
    postinst lays 2770 (setgid) down at the state root, but the next
    service start re-asserts RuntimeDirectory/StateDirectoryMode from the
    RUNNING systemd cache — observed live on 0.1.0+pkg2 (VM
    2026-10-20): stale cached 0750 reset the tree to 0750 at start, so
    every upgrade-side permission change was stomped at boot ("none of
    the patches landed"). postinst now ends with an explicit guarded
    `systemctl daemon-reload` (dh_installsystemd normally does this;
    belt-and-braces so a unit-file change can never be restarted-over).
  * Legacy tree file modes: top-level state files with pre-UMask modes
    (ids.db 0640) stay group-read-only after any upgrade — operator
    SQLite writes die with "attempt to write a readonly database". The
    postinst legacy-tree pass now reconciles top-level file modes to
    g+rw as well as ownership.
  * Brain socket stops widening the lane behind the unit's back: the
    unconditional socket-dir chmod 0777 + umask-0 bind (socket 0777
    world-connectable) is replaced by lane-aware shaping — group-shared
    dirs get socket 0770/lock 0660 (operator group connects), legacy
    world-shared container dirs keep 0777/0666, owner-only dev dirs get
    0700/0600. The unit's 0770 RuntimeDirectory shape is now honored
    instead of being overwritten at Brain start.
  * framework_health findings_db: the generic "could not create/open"
    branch carries the real exception text (a chromadb import error used
    to masquerade as a DB permission problem).

 -- Surzal-kali <vgreenwald@student.cnm.edu>  Mon, 20 Oct 2026 16:20:00 -0600

daharness (0.1.0+pkg2) kali; urgency=high

  * F1, gateway auth armable from the package: conffile gains
    GATEWAY_API_KEY (postinst generates a random key when the
    placeholder is empty) and GATEWAY_HOST (system profile pin,
    127.0.0.1); bootstrap GATEWAY_HOST/GATEWAY_PORT knobs replace the
    hardcoded 0.0.0.0:5000 (loopback default, ZAP pattern); api_gateway
    logs a boot-time error on unauthenticated + non-loopback binds.
  * F2, /etc/daharness/daharness.env is now live: EnvironmentFile= on
    the daemon + kernel units (chroma already read it); the inert
    Environment=DAHARNESS_ENV and duplicate BRAIN_SOCKET unit lines are
    dropped, so daemon/kernel/chroma all resolve WORKSPACE_ROOT through
    the StateDirectory-conffile chain.
  * F3/F4/F5: daharness-safety(7) bind + auth posture section;
    daharness.env(5) LOADING section rewritten to the implemented wiring;
    .env.example OPEN_TERMINAL residue dropped; runbook Python-3.13
    blurb refreshed to 3.14 and step-9 gateway smoke carries the API key.
  * Optional engagement-Postgres lane: /usr/bin/daharness-pg
    (init|start|stop|status) provisions a dedicated 'daharness' cluster
    on 5433 (msfdb's main cluster on 5432 untouched), creates the harness
    db + lane roles from the now-installed init bundle, and writes
    per-lane passwords to root:daharness 0640 /etc/daharness/pg.env
    (daharness-pg.1). Units gain tolerant EnvironmentFile=-pg.env; conffile
    documents HARNESS_DB_* knobs; postgresql added to Suggests. Lane is
    inert until an operator runs daharness-pg init.
  * Secretary chat lane trimmed for the headless build: bootstrap's
    interactive branch (secretary _chat + boot-time indexing) is removed,
    bare `daharness` now foregrounds the services stack exactly like
    --daemon; SECRETARY_MODEL dropped from /etc/daharness/daharness.env
    (no packaged lane reads it; EMBED_MODEL/OLLAMA_BASE_URL stay for the
    registry/memory lanes). The driving LLM headless is external
    (Open WebUI / gateway client); daharness-tools(7) rewritten.
  Follow-up: daharness-index(1) — the operator re-index wrapper (the
  runbook's discovery smoke would otherwise hit an empty registry).
  * packaging repair (VM 2026-10-20): replkit/ was missing from the
    staged tree, so daharness-repl and the kernel unit died instantly
    with "No module named replkit" (tool_repl imports it top-level);
    the tree-copy loop now stages replkit alongside the other packages.
  (evasion/ was never missing — it has been in the tree-copy set since
  pkg1; its absence would fail discovery coverage, not imports.)
  * teardown repair: _child_log_fds AttributeError killed
    daharness.service on a fresh install. stop()'s reap popped the
    child-log-fd table directly, but registration is lazy at the spawn
    sites; on a deb where ZAP's launcher is absent and MSF is not
    installed, the Brain is the only child and (until now) also
    registered nothing, so any teardown (SIGTERM or the finally after a
    launch error) died with AttributeError, masking the original error.
    The reap is now getattr-tolerant and the Brain's spawn site
    registers its /tmp/brain.log fd like the MSF/ZAP/Playwright sites
    (closes a standing fd leak too).
  * teardown repair 2 (VM 2026-10-20): systemd's KillMode=process leaves
    child hygiene entirely to stop(), and signal handlers were installed
    only AFTER launch_all — with ZAP absent, wait_for_zap burned 60s
    before handlers existed, so systemctl stop/restart mid-upgrade hit
    Python's default SIGTERM: instant main death, no reap, orphaned
    Brain/msfrpcd on live sockets ("State 'stop-sigterm' timed out",
    left-over-process warnings on every later start). SIGTERM/SIGINT
    handlers + the shutdown event now install before launch; the ZAP
    launcher-absent branch marks the wait as answerable so launch is
    not held 60s on a machine with no ZAP. A TERM arriving mid-boot now
    races the launch: the remainder is abandoned and stop() reaps what
    already exists (verified: stop mid-launch completes in ~1s with
    ExecMainStatus=0 instead of systemd's 30s SIGKILL).
  * msfrpcd orphan fix (VM 2026-10-20): msfrpcd self-daemonizes, so the
    tracked launcher exited immediately and the ruby daemon reparented
    to PID 1, surviving every stop() reap (one fresh PPID-1 msfrpcd per
    boot cycle). msfrpcd now spawns with -f (foreground) like every other
    child; stop() reaps it with the same SIGTERM-then-SIGKILL path
    (verified: all children gone after stop, zero left-over-process
    warnings).
  * ZAP launch fix for the deb lane (VM 2026-10-20): zap_home (the daemon's
    -dir) was created under framework_root, but the service runs as user
    'daharness' while /usr/share/daharness is root-owned — mkdir failed
    with PermissionError BEFORE any log line, the coroutine died silently
    and wait_for_zap burned its 60s on a daemon that never started. The
    fallback path is $ZAP_HOME env, else <state dir>/.zap_home
    (/var/lib/daharness/.zap_home); ZAP now comes up and is reaped with
    everything else.

